WEBVTT

00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:41.292
The time will soon be at hand.

00:00:41.292 --> 00:00:45.250
Right now, you need
only remain in slumber...

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:50.583
...until the time comes
for us to display our fury...

00:01:13.708 --> 00:01:20.375
<i>we wanna be there even if we had to</i>
<i>twist the world all around to get there</i>

00:01:20.375 --> 00:01:31.208
<i>without you, i guess i couldn't</i>
<i>even find the future here today</i>

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:42.250
<i>i was always trying to take nothing for granted</i>

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:50.250
<i>for the day i might lose them</i>

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:57.250
<i>but you just came in to my black</i>
<i>and white monochrome destiny</i>

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:07.458
<i>and colored it all over</i>

00:02:08.292 --> 00:02:14.833
<i>we won't be satisfied with the routine future</i>

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:22.292
<i>we were born to make a new history come true</i>

00:02:22.292 --> 00:02:29.458
<i>there's absolutely no</i>
<i>absolute thing in this world</i>

00:02:29.458 --> 00:02:34.042
<i>this road goes on forever</i>

00:02:34.042 --> 00:02:40.125
<i>as long as we won't give up</i>

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.917
"Nice Day for a Death Bazaar!"

00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:48.500
I see...

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.750
If there is a witch directing
them behind the scenes,

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.708
you suspect one of those three, then?

00:02:52.708 --> 00:02:56.458
Yes. These last Traitor
incidents have been perpetrated

00:02:56.458 --> 00:02:58.917
by law-abiding citizens who
suddenly change.

00:02:58.917 --> 00:03:00.667
If a witch were involved,

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:04.875
I figured it would be
one with skill in mind control.

00:03:04.875 --> 00:03:08.167
What about this witch, Arachne,
that you have singled out here?

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:11.333
That witch is skilled in the
development of Magic Tools,

00:03:11.333 --> 00:03:15.167
and appears to have tried creating
Magic Tools to brainwash people,

00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:18.500
but on further inspection, she seems
to have perished 800 years ago.

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:21.333
Besides which,
these Traitors all display

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:23.958
the peculiarity of not sleeping.

00:03:23.958 --> 00:03:27.458
Through depriving them of sleep,
their sense of fear is lost,

00:03:27.458 --> 00:03:29.333
and by casting mind control on them,

00:03:29.333 --> 00:03:31.958
they can create soldiers who never rest.

00:03:31.958 --> 00:03:33.417
As for those without
any martial arts experience,

00:03:33.417 --> 00:03:36.292
we think they have been
expanding the abilities of people

00:03:36.292 --> 00:03:38.375
who aren't particularly physically gifted

00:03:38.375 --> 00:03:42.458
by performing some kind
of special doping on them.

00:03:42.458 --> 00:03:44.958
They would indeed be the ideal soldiers.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:47.708
Mm-hmm. And after you
followed that line of reasoning

00:03:47.708 --> 00:03:49.167
and started checking backgrounds,

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.708
the most likely suspect was that witch,

00:03:51.708 --> 00:03:53.792
Shaula Gorgon.

00:03:53.792 --> 00:03:55.625
This is, after all, merely conjecture.

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:59.875
Witches are crafty.
Even if we know who the culprit is,

00:03:59.875 --> 00:04:02.750
tracking them down is still the hard part.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.542
Even so, well spotted, Clay.
A witch's record is often cryptic,

00:04:08.542 --> 00:04:12.583
and rather than just a decade or two,
they go back for centuries.

00:04:12.583 --> 00:04:16.125
They need those like you,
who have elevated analytical skills,

00:04:16.125 --> 00:04:18.250
here at Central Intelligence.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:19.792
Thanks.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:20.917
What's one plus one?

00:04:20.917 --> 00:04:25.333
Eh? W-Why are you asking me,
out of the blue?! Let's see...

00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:27.708
Two! It's two, of course!

00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:29.625
A bit slow on the uptake, though.

00:04:29.625 --> 00:04:31.125
Oh, be quiet!

00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:35.500
Well, that's where you, the cool,
collected Akane, must support him.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.250
Meister and weapon are two in one.

00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:42.167
Geez, we came the
way you said to, Miss Meme,

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:43.625
and now we're lost, aren't we?

00:04:43.625 --> 00:04:47.708
As I recall, Miss Anya, you were
the one who suggested a shortcut.

00:04:47.708 --> 00:04:49.667
That's because we have
a study session, Miss Meme,

00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:51.292
and you forgot your textbook.

00:04:51.292 --> 00:04:55.917
Now, now, you two. It's an "underground" shortcut. Get it?
[<i>chika</i>: underground] [<i>chikamichi</i>: shortcut]

00:04:58.417 --> 00:05:02.583
I am going this way. Miss Tsugumi,
you're coming this way too, right?

00:05:02.583 --> 00:05:03.292
Huh?

00:05:03.292 --> 00:05:06.875
I think it's <i>that </i>way.
What about you, Tsugumi?

00:05:06.875 --> 00:05:10.458
Well... Let's see...

00:05:10.458 --> 00:05:12.125
I think...

00:05:12.125 --> 00:05:13.708
--Tsugumi!
--Miss Tsugumi!

00:05:15.625 --> 00:05:19.625
Ah! I wonder if there's someone in that room!

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.542
Yes?

00:05:23.208 --> 00:05:25.458
Please excuse us. Huh?

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:26.208
Oh!

00:05:26.208 --> 00:05:27.125
Hey there.

00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:29.833
What are you all doing here?

00:05:29.833 --> 00:05:32.792
Oh, uh... How can I say this?

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:35.917
I was telling Sid-<i>sensei </i>that I like him--

00:05:35.917 --> 00:05:39.125
Sid-<i>sensei </i>asked us to
pick up some snacks for him.

00:05:39.125 --> 00:05:41.333
Sorry for putting you out like that.

00:05:41.333 --> 00:05:42.458
Is that right?

00:05:42.458 --> 00:05:44.958
Yes! Yes, yes. Mm-hmm.

00:05:44.958 --> 00:05:47.333
By the way, what are you doing here?

00:05:47.333 --> 00:05:49.792
As it happens, while we were
on our way back to the classroom

00:05:49.792 --> 00:05:52.667
to get something we forgot, we got lost.

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:57.250
DWMA is set up like a maze,
in order to keep its secrets.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.750
It's Miss Tsugumi's fault.

00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:03.375
It's because she can't choose
a route or a partner that we're lost.

00:06:03.375 --> 00:06:05.833
She's right, Miss Tsugumi.

00:06:05.833 --> 00:06:07.458
You, too, Meme?

00:06:07.458 --> 00:06:10.208
Oh, you haven't picked a partner yet?

00:06:10.917 --> 00:06:13.542
There are some meisters
who have two weapons,

00:06:13.542 --> 00:06:17.167
but I've never heard of one weapon
having two different meisters.

00:06:23.125 --> 00:06:25.167
You're afraid that whichever
partner you choose,

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:28.500
it's going to end up
hurting the other one, right?

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:32.375
Harudori, you've got a kind heart.

00:06:33.458 --> 00:06:35.458
Mr. Akane, it's because you
say that sort of thing

00:06:35.458 --> 00:06:38.542
that Miss Tsugumi is
having trouble deciding, isn't it?

00:06:39.292 --> 00:06:42.417
She could always
choose someone besides you two.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.667
Hey! You guys are lost, right?
I'll get you back upstairs!

00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:49.042
Oh, that's right!

00:06:49.042 --> 00:06:50.458
The study session!

00:07:00.375 --> 00:07:03.833
Hmm... I'm bored.

00:07:03.833 --> 00:07:06.042
There're no customers.

00:07:06.042 --> 00:07:09.875
I guess no one wants to
look at your sulky face, Master.

00:07:09.875 --> 00:07:13.042
If only you could tell a joke.

00:07:13.042 --> 00:07:15.333
A joke, huh?

00:07:15.333 --> 00:07:18.917
Long ago, my entire family was killed,

00:07:18.917 --> 00:07:22.250
and ever since, I've been unable to laugh.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.750
I'm joking.

00:07:26.792 --> 00:07:28.958
Nobody's gonna get that!

00:07:28.958 --> 00:07:32.542
It was just my daughter that was killed.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:37.292
I'm joking. I never married.

00:07:40.792 --> 00:07:42.333
Hello!

00:07:42.583 --> 00:07:43.417
Welcome.

00:07:43.417 --> 00:07:46.208
Yo! We saved your seats for you.

00:07:46.208 --> 00:07:49.083
Wow! Thank you so much!

00:07:49.083 --> 00:07:52.708
But from the looks of it,
there was no need to make a reservation.

00:07:52.708 --> 00:07:54.125
No way!

00:07:54.125 --> 00:07:56.625
I don't wanna!
I don't wanna! I don't wanna!

00:07:56.625 --> 00:07:57.625
Come on!

00:07:57.625 --> 00:08:02.625
We came all this way to look
after your studies, so let's do it!

00:08:05.292 --> 00:08:08.542
It's no surprise that Miss Jackie's
notes are well-organized,

00:08:08.542 --> 00:08:10.125
and easy to follow, is it?

00:08:10.125 --> 00:08:13.000
Easy to follow? Which part?

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.458
Stop your complaining and concentrate.

00:08:15.458 --> 00:08:19.083
You're going to have to break
down and memorize the basics by heart.

00:08:19.083 --> 00:08:22.792
Miss Meme can remember
everything covered by the test.

00:08:22.792 --> 00:08:25.250
Huh? There's going to be a test on this?

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:27.583
What did you think
today's get-together was for?

00:08:27.583 --> 00:08:29.500
Oh, of course!

00:08:30.208 --> 00:08:31.125
'Sup?

00:08:31.125 --> 00:08:33.417
We came to take your orders.

00:08:33.417 --> 00:08:35.458
I'll have a royal milk tea, please.

00:08:35.458 --> 00:08:36.958
Iced café au lait!

00:08:36.958 --> 00:08:38.500
A cappuccino for me.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.208
Iced lemon tea, please.

00:08:40.208 --> 00:08:42.500
I'll have an iced café mocha.

00:08:43.583 --> 00:08:47.000
We'll just bring enough
of whatever for all of you.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.042
What, again?

00:08:49.583 --> 00:08:52.500
Aw, Jackie, you're
such a straight-laced chick,

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.917
I'm surprised you're not better at teaching.

00:08:54.917 --> 00:08:58.292
What can I say?
You just don't have a knack for it.

00:08:58.292 --> 00:09:00.125
Not to mention being dreadful.

00:09:00.125 --> 00:09:02.833
Then why don't you have Ox teach you?

00:09:02.833 --> 00:09:03.750
Huh?

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:07.417
He'd be glad to spoon-feed a
selfish <i>tanuki </i>like you.

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:11.208
And while you're at it, you could
stand to learn some discipline.

00:09:11.208 --> 00:09:15.958
Okay, fine. I'll put up
with the straight-laced chick.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:21.250
What's with the look?!
You're pissing me off!

00:09:23.458 --> 00:09:24.458
There you go.

00:09:24.458 --> 00:09:26.958
That is what you all wanted to drink, right?

00:09:26.958 --> 00:09:29.542
Lately, I've gotten so
I can tell what a customer will order

00:09:29.542 --> 00:09:33.458
by the look on their face. This is perfect.

00:09:44.375 --> 00:09:45.792
You wouldn't have a prayer!

00:09:45.792 --> 00:09:47.000
Oh, yeah? Just watch me!

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.208
Go ahead and try it!

00:09:51.375 --> 00:09:52.917
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:09:52.917 --> 00:09:56.542
Shut up! You're thinking of
going into EAT with that kind of control?

00:09:56.542 --> 00:09:58.708
Shut up, you! I've got plenty of control!

00:09:58.708 --> 00:10:00.458
--Ha-ha, not a chance!
--What's with them?!

00:10:00.458 --> 00:10:04.792
They're DWMA students. There are
many who gain some skills in NOT,

00:10:04.792 --> 00:10:07.625
and then start getting the wrong ideas.

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:12.042
Since Tsugumi and the others
are here today, let's leave them alone.

00:10:12.042 --> 00:10:14.792
Hey, you're bothering the other customers.

00:10:14.792 --> 00:10:15.750
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:17.917
What's your problem?
We're customers, here!

00:10:17.917 --> 00:10:21.125
Don't go acting so tough,
or I'll send you to the hospital.

00:10:21.125 --> 00:10:24.917
Huh? Don't get too full of yourself,
just because you're a girl--

00:10:34.625 --> 00:10:36.167
Let's go.

00:10:42.375 --> 00:10:44.292
Hey, waitress!

00:10:44.292 --> 00:10:46.625
Just wait! I'm coming!

00:10:48.792 --> 00:10:51.625
It's getting full-blown busy, huh?

00:10:51.625 --> 00:10:53.125
I know!

00:10:53.125 --> 00:10:54.625
Master!

00:10:54.958 --> 00:10:56.750
We'll give you a hand.

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.792
Do we have to wear <i>that </i>again?

00:10:58.792 --> 00:10:59.833
Eh?

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.667
<i>That</i>?

00:11:03.792 --> 00:11:05.833
What are you doing, Jackie?

00:11:05.833 --> 00:11:10.125
Hmm, I kind of want to try it on.

00:11:11.083 --> 00:11:12.958
I'll pass.

00:11:14.292 --> 00:11:19.292
Master, any work back here?
And by the way, I <i>will </i>be getting paid.

00:11:19.292 --> 00:11:21.292
Well, could I get you
to cut up those lemons?

00:11:21.292 --> 00:11:24.000
Huh? Kim, ma'am,
you're not wearing a uniform?

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:25.708
I'm sure you'd look good in it.

00:11:25.708 --> 00:11:27.667
You can just pipe down.

00:11:34.333 --> 00:11:36.792
This is definitely too short!

00:11:39.375 --> 00:11:41.583
Jacqueline, ma'am, you look cute.

00:11:41.583 --> 00:11:42.333
I do?

00:11:42.333 --> 00:11:44.583
Wow! How slender!

00:11:44.583 --> 00:11:48.208
Not really.
I mean, Tsugumi, you are, too...

00:11:48.333 --> 00:11:52.000
But <i>I </i>happen to be petite all over.

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:58.667
Master, we're ready!

00:11:58.667 --> 00:12:00.458
What would you like us to do?

00:12:00.458 --> 00:12:03.625
Whoo, I'm exhausted.

00:12:03.625 --> 00:12:04.667
Just as I thought,

00:12:04.667 --> 00:12:07.208
we only happened to be busy for a bit.

00:12:07.208 --> 00:12:08.167
Huh?

00:12:08.167 --> 00:12:10.833
You could have said something
<i>before </i>we got changed!

00:12:10.833 --> 00:12:15.042
But it's so nice to
see you in those uniforms.

00:12:15.167 --> 00:12:16.875
Still, everything is okay.

00:12:16.875 --> 00:12:18.875
Yes, it is. We can just blow off time

00:12:18.875 --> 00:12:21.958
when there are no
customers around, like always.

00:12:21.958 --> 00:12:24.167
It isn't right to say that.

00:12:24.875 --> 00:12:28.708
However, you are right;
the usual pace is more relaxing.

00:12:36.417 --> 00:12:38.958
Everyone left already, right?

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:48.917
--Gah!
--Why, you little!

00:13:13.875 --> 00:13:16.917
♪ Death Bazaar! ♪

00:13:16.917 --> 00:13:18.458
♪ Death Ba-- ♪

00:13:18.458 --> 00:13:19.833
♪ Death-- ♪

00:13:19.833 --> 00:13:22.167
What's going on?

00:13:22.167 --> 00:13:25.667
Miss Tsugumi, have you ever
heard of the Death Bazaar?

00:13:25.667 --> 00:13:27.083
Death Bazaar?

00:13:27.083 --> 00:13:30.958
They appear to be holding one,
at Death Pain Square.

00:13:30.958 --> 00:13:33.667
People open their
own shops inside the plaza,

00:13:33.667 --> 00:13:36.708
bring their old things in,
and sell them, I hear.

00:13:36.792 --> 00:13:38.917
Are you talking about a flea market?

00:13:38.917 --> 00:13:42.958
That's my Miss Tsugumi!
You know all about poor people things!

00:13:42.958 --> 00:13:45.208
Miss Tsugumi,
I thought you might want to go, so...

00:13:45.208 --> 00:13:47.958
Huh? No, not really.

00:13:51.167 --> 00:13:52.750
I-I see...

00:13:53.125 --> 00:13:58.167
Ah! Actually, I'm generally
acknowledged to enjoy flea markets,

00:13:58.167 --> 00:13:58.917
and I was thinking,

00:13:58.917 --> 00:14:02.542
I'd love to take the opportunity
to find some bargains...

00:14:03.292 --> 00:14:05.625
Well, there, you see?

00:14:07.292 --> 00:14:10.250
That smile isn't fighting fair.

00:14:22.667 --> 00:14:27.500
Get this katana, with which I have
slain six evildoers, for just $25!

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:29.833
I've got the 6mm shell casing from the round

00:14:29.833 --> 00:14:32.958
that assassinated Mafia Don Springcherry.

00:14:32.958 --> 00:14:35.375
So this is a flea market?

00:14:35.375 --> 00:14:38.250
Yes. It's pretty wild here.

00:14:40.708 --> 00:14:43.208
Please buy something!

00:14:43.208 --> 00:14:47.708
These are my own clothes!
I'll discount them as much as you like!

00:14:47.708 --> 00:14:49.500
Eternal Feather, ma'am...

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:52.208
You're open for business?

00:14:52.875 --> 00:14:54.625
Step right on up.

00:14:54.625 --> 00:14:55.542
Huh?

00:14:57.792 --> 00:14:59.417
These are just...

00:14:59.417 --> 00:15:00.958
What awful fashion sense, huh?

00:15:00.958 --> 00:15:02.250
Please, don't misunderstand!

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:06.292
These are clothes that
Miss Kim tricked me into buying!

00:15:06.292 --> 00:15:09.000
I want to sell these clothes,
and buy some clothes that I can wear

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:11.417
to go shopping for more fancy clothes.

00:15:11.417 --> 00:15:14.167
So please, buy these clo--

00:15:18.292 --> 00:15:23.417
Please buy something.
These are my own clothes.

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:27.792
Hi there.

00:15:34.583 --> 00:15:39.708
Hmm, there's a lot here,
but not really anything I want, you know?

00:15:42.083 --> 00:15:43.875
Oh, my! How lovely!

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.708
I guess if you enjoy it,
Miss Anya, it's all right.

00:15:50.958 --> 00:15:53.083
Is this a garbage dump?

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.417
If you keep scaring
away customers with that look,

00:15:56.417 --> 00:15:57.917
you don't stand a
chance of selling anything!

00:15:57.917 --> 00:15:59.667
I always have this look on my face!

00:15:59.667 --> 00:16:03.458
Stop screwing around!
You just don't want to sell your books, right?

00:16:03.458 --> 00:16:05.417
But you'll chuck out my things like crazy.

00:16:05.417 --> 00:16:07.042
If you're not gonna
read the books, sell them!

00:16:07.042 --> 00:16:08.958
There's no room in our place to keep them!

00:16:08.958 --> 00:16:11.917
Shut up! That's why we're here, right?!

00:16:11.917 --> 00:16:14.083
Um, about those books...

00:16:14.583 --> 00:16:17.625
You jerk! Come on, smile! Come on!

00:16:17.875 --> 00:16:19.792
Maka, ma'am, hello.

00:16:20.667 --> 00:16:21.625
Hey!

00:16:21.625 --> 00:16:22.625
Huh?

00:16:22.792 --> 00:16:24.708
Wow. Books, huh?

00:16:24.708 --> 00:16:26.542
Sell them. They're just in the way.

00:16:26.542 --> 00:16:27.583
Nyah!

00:16:27.583 --> 00:16:32.083
Oh, that book! I read that
book just as I was starting school,

00:16:32.083 --> 00:16:34.375
at the same time you're at now, Tsugumi.

00:16:34.542 --> 00:16:35.958
Oh, yeah?

00:16:35.958 --> 00:16:37.583
Is that right?

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:40.417
Tsugumi, you like books?

00:16:40.417 --> 00:16:43.750
Huh? Oh, yes.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:47.167
Okay. Well, you can have that book.

00:16:47.167 --> 00:16:49.458
Huh? No, I couldn't!

00:16:49.458 --> 00:16:53.000
In return, just read it carefully.

00:16:54.292 --> 00:16:57.083
Thank you very much!
I will treasure reading it!

00:16:57.083 --> 00:16:59.875
Ugh, <i>finally</i>, one of them.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.333
Miss Anya! Meme!

00:17:05.333 --> 00:17:08.500
Oh, Miss Tsugumi. Where have you been?

00:17:10.875 --> 00:17:13.292
Why is she smiling like that?

00:17:14.125 --> 00:17:15.958
Please help me.

00:17:16.333 --> 00:17:18.708
Please help me.

00:17:21.667 --> 00:17:24.167
Maybe I should give up and go home.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.125
Wow...

00:17:30.125 --> 00:17:31.833
Step right up.

00:17:32.375 --> 00:17:35.292
All of these accessories
have a scorpion motif, huh?

00:17:35.292 --> 00:17:36.667
Yes.

00:17:36.667 --> 00:17:39.542
I'm a Scorpio myself, and I want
to be the sort of mysterious woman

00:17:39.542 --> 00:17:42.250
who can beguile others at first bite.

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:43.958
Well then...

00:17:43.958 --> 00:17:46.292
...what about this one?

00:17:46.792 --> 00:17:48.125
That's fantastic!

00:17:48.125 --> 00:17:50.833
The price is reasonable, too.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:52.875
I'll take it!

00:17:54.208 --> 00:17:56.250
Shall I put it on you?

00:17:56.542 --> 00:17:57.667
Here...

00:17:57.667 --> 00:17:59.042
Okay.

00:18:09.208 --> 00:18:10.292
Ow!

00:18:10.875 --> 00:18:13.375
Are you all right, miss?

00:18:15.375 --> 00:18:16.875
Yes...

00:18:16.875 --> 00:18:20.375
I... am... fine...

00:18:49.583 --> 00:18:51.500
I'm glad we came.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:53.542
Well, there, you see?

00:18:53.542 --> 00:18:56.208
What should we go look at next?

00:19:20.167 --> 00:19:22.000
Are you okay, Tsugumi?!

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:23.458
Mm-hmm...

00:19:28.792 --> 00:19:31.292
Eternal Feather, ma'am...?

00:19:36.917 --> 00:19:38.417
Those eyes...

00:19:44.958 --> 00:19:48.333
Your bag will be cut in half!
Dodge to the side!

00:19:53.292 --> 00:19:55.167
What are you doing?

00:19:55.792 --> 00:19:58.458
You're a DWMA student, right?

00:20:09.333 --> 00:20:10.583
Watch out!

00:20:14.917 --> 00:20:18.167
I won't let you touch my meister.

00:20:19.958 --> 00:20:23.667
I should have been
there to protect Miss Anya.

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:25.958
You know her?

00:20:25.958 --> 00:20:28.458
Yes. She's one of our NOT class seniors.

00:20:28.458 --> 00:20:30.708
Eternal Feather, ma'am!

00:20:33.208 --> 00:20:35.792
It doesn't look like she can hear you.

00:20:42.958 --> 00:20:47.625
We can't allow her to get hurt.
Soul, we can't attack her.

00:20:47.625 --> 00:20:48.833
Gotcha.

00:20:54.208 --> 00:20:57.708
Don't resist!
We don't want to hurt you!

00:20:57.708 --> 00:21:00.750
Miss Feather!
Let's talk about what happened!

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:03.042
Eternal Feather, ma'am!

00:21:05.958 --> 00:21:08.167
If this keeps up,
we'll just do more damage.

00:21:08.167 --> 00:21:09.667
Let's bring her under control, Soul.

00:21:09.667 --> 00:21:11.083
Here goes!

00:21:14.792 --> 00:21:16.917
It looks like an EAT
pair have come to their aid.

00:21:16.917 --> 00:21:20.000
If they're facing a single weapon,
they should be fine.

00:21:20.917 --> 00:21:23.250
Sure enough, with that amount of venom,

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:27.167
it would be difficult
to compete with an EAT meister.

00:21:27.542 --> 00:21:30.042
But her being in NOT aside,

00:21:30.042 --> 00:21:35.000
it was so easy to take control
of a strong-willed DWMA student.

00:21:35.458 --> 00:21:37.125
Letting the subject be apprehended

00:21:37.125 --> 00:21:39.708
and investigated would be problematic.

00:21:39.708 --> 00:21:42.583
All right. Let's end this by seeing

00:21:42.583 --> 00:21:47.333
just how far the brainwashing will
allow me to command her.

00:21:48.167 --> 00:21:50.042
Kill yourself.

00:22:09.208 --> 00:22:10.250
Don't do it!

00:22:25.708 --> 00:22:28.875
Hurry and get some help!
Everyone, help me stop the bleeding!

00:22:28.875 --> 00:22:31.500
Get something to hold against this wound!

00:22:31.500 --> 00:22:34.667
What do we do?!
We can't stop the bleeding!

00:22:47.542 --> 00:22:51.708
<i>With a big wave and a "See you,"</i>

00:22:51.708 --> 00:22:58.625
<i>let's meet in the new day</i>

00:23:15.375 --> 00:23:19.542
<i>Our shadows stretch along the pavement</i>

00:23:19.542 --> 00:23:23.542
<i>coming together, then apart, then together</i>

00:23:23.542 --> 00:23:31.875
<i>What do I say when the road home ends?</i>

00:23:31.875 --> 00:23:36.042
<i>You are not alone. Nope, right nearby,</i>

00:23:36.042 --> 00:23:40.167
<i>there are eyes looking back at you</i>

00:23:40.167 --> 00:23:44.292
<i>And just like a miracle,</i>

00:23:44.292 --> 00:23:48.042
<i>they can turn even failures into laughter</i>

00:23:48.042 --> 00:23:52.167
<i>Thank you for a fun day</i>

00:23:52.167 --> 00:23:56.500
<i>Let's do it again tomorrow</i>

00:23:56.500 --> 00:24:00.583
<i>We'll open a brand-new door</i>

00:24:00.583 --> 00:24:04.750
<i>chasing after dreams and love</i>

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:10.375
<i>and those nameless feelings, too</i>

00:24:17.708 --> 00:24:21.667
Tsugumi, the day will come
when you will choose your partner.

00:24:21.667 --> 00:24:23.667
Either myself, or Miss Anya.

00:24:23.667 --> 00:24:26.917
Miss Tsugumi, you don't have
a blade because you have no resolve!

00:24:26.917 --> 00:24:28.917
He's got a screw in his head!

00:24:28.917 --> 00:24:32.150
"Next time: Tsugumi Spiral!"
Ultimately, only one person can make the decision.
